## if/else
Sometimes you need your code to make decisions. `if` checks a condition - if it's true, the code inside runs. If it's false, the `else` block runs instead.

```qc
int x = 10;
if (x > 5) {
    println("Big");
} else {
    println("Small");
}
// prints: Big
```

### How it works:
- `if` evaluates the condition inside `()`
- If true, runs the first `{}` block
- If false, runs the `else {}` block
- `else` is optional - you can use `if` alone

```qc
int x = 10;
if (x > 100) {
    println("This never runs");
}
println("This always runs");
```


